I also suggest making `allPluginsCache` have `null` as initial value, and then it should be assigned a promise.

that way if `allPlugins` is called in parallel, a race condition will not happen

e.g.

```typescript
let allPluginsCache = null;
export const allPlugins = async () => {
    if (allPluginsCache) return await allPluginsCache;

    const { promise, resolve } = Promise.withResolvers();
    allPluginsCache = promise;

    const plugins = await Promise.all([
        import("..../synced-lyrics/index.ts").then(plg => ["synced-lyrics", plg]),
        import("....").then(plg => ["xy", plg]),
    ]);

    resolve(plugins.reduce((acc, [name, plg]) => ({ ...acc,  [name]: plg  }), {}));
    return await promise;
};
```
